{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' screening_policy.md && wc -l customers.csv dev/customers_dev.csv dev/labels_dev.csv && sed -n '1,16p' customers.csv && sed -n '1,20p' dev/customers_dev.csv && sed -n '1,30p' dev/labels_dev.csv && python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='watchlist.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint(type(d), len(d) if hasattr(d,'__len__') else None)\nif isinstance(d,dict):\n print(d.keys())\n vals=next((v for v in d.values() if isinstance(v,list)),None)\n print('list len',len(vals) if vals is not None else None)\n for x in (vals or [])[:4]: print(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nelse:\n for x in d[:4]: print(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' screening_policy.md && wc -l customers.csv dev/customers_dev.csv dev/labels_dev.csv && sed -n '1,16p' customers.csv && sed -n '1,20p' dev/customers_dev.csv && sed -n '1,30p' dev/labels_dev.csv && python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='watchlist.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint(type(d), len(d) if hasattr(d,'__len__') else None)\nif isinstance(d,dict):\n print(d.keys())\n vals=next((v for v in d.values() if isinstance(v,list)),None)\n print('list len',len(vals) if vals is not None else None)\n for x in (vals or [])[:4]: print(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nelse:\n for x in d[:4]: print(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Sanctions Screening Policy\n\nThis policy defines when a customer record matches a watchlist entry. The\nverifier grades outcomes only: for every customer in `/app/customers.csv`,\n`decision` must be `MATCH` with the correct `matched_uid`, or `NO_MATCH`.\n\n## Inputs\n\n`/app/watchlist.json` is a list of entries with `uid`, `type`\n(`individual`, `entity`, `vessel`), `primary_name`, `script_name` (the name in\nits original script when the person is from an Arabic-, Persian- or\nCyrillic-script culture, else null), `aliases` (each with `name` and\n`strength` `strong` or `weak`), `dob` (`YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY`, or empty),\n`nationalities`, `ids` (each with `type` and `number`) and `programs`. For some\nindividuals `primary_name` is the original-script name itself; those entries\nmay have no Latin spelling anywhere.\n\n`/app/customers.csv` has `customer_id, full_name, dob, nationality, id_type,\nid_number, type`. `dob` may be a full date, a year, a year-month, or empty.\n\n## Rule 1: identifiers\n\nIf the customer's `id_type` and `id_number` equal an entry's identifier\n(`passport`, `registration`, or `imo`), the customer matches that entry\nregardless of the name or date of birth.\n\n## Rule 2: name equivalence\n\nTwo names refer to the same person when, after normalization, the given name\nand the family name correspond. Names correspond across all of the following\nvariations, which the batch and the development sample contain:\n\n- Transliteration into Latin script from Arabic, Persian and Cyrillic under any\n  common romanization (for example Muhammad/Mohammed/Mohamed/Mohamad,\n  Abdul Rahman/Abdurrahman/Abd al-Rahman, Hussein/Husain/Hussain/Husayn,\n  Sergei/Sergey/Serguei/Sergej, Fedorov/Fyodorov/Fedoroff, Yevgeny/Evgeny/Eugene),\n  including matching a Latin customer name against an entry that only has an\n  original-script name.\n- Chinese names under pinyin and Wade-Giles/Cantonese romanizations\n  (Zhang/Chang, Wang/Wong, Li/Lee, Zhou/Chou/Chow, Xiao Ming/Xiaoming/Hsiao-Ming),\n  in either family-name-first or given-name-first order.\n- Western nicknames and diacritic variants (William/Bill, Katherine/Kate,\n  Jose/José, Mueller/Müller/Muller, Nguyen/Nguyễn), middle initials, and\n  hyphenated versus spaced compound surnames.\n- Name order (family name first, with or without a comma), presence or absence\n  of Russian patronymics, presence or absence of Arabic nasab elements\n  (`bin`/`ibn`/`ben` + father's name), and presence or absence of the Arabic\n  article (`al-`, `el-`, `Al `, attached `Al`).\n- Feminine Russian surname forms (Ivanova/Ivanov).\n\nNames do not correspond when the given name or the family name is a different\nname (Hassan is not Hussein, Ahmadi is not Ahmadi-with-a-different-given-name,\nAl-Noor Trading is not Al-Noor Shipping). A single shared given name or a\nsingle shared family name is not a name match.\n\n## Rule 3: aliases\n\nA `strong` alias is an alternative name of the entry and participates in\nRule 2 exactly like `primary_name`. A `weak` alias (a nickname or nom de\nguerre) matches a customer only when the customer's name equals the alias and\nRule 4 corroborates with an identical full date of birth, or Rule 1 applies.\nA weak alias alone never produces a match.\n\n## Rule 4: date of birth\n\nDates of birth are compared only when both sides have one. A full customer\ndate must equal the entry's full date. A customer year or year-month must be\na prefix of the entry's date. Any disagreement rules the candidate out (the\ncustomer is a different person with a similar name). A missing date on either\nside neither confirms nor rules out.\n\n## Rule 5: entities and vessels\n\nEntity names correspond when all name words correspond after removing legal\nform designators (LLC, L.L.C., Limited Liability Company, Ltd, Limited, S.A.,\nGmbH, JSC, Joint Stock Company, AO, OAO, PJSC, Co., Company, FZE, FZ-LLC and\nsimilar), leading `The`, punctuation, and the words `and`/`&`; case is\nignored. Vessel names correspond after removing prefixes such as `M/V`, `MV`,\n`M/T`, `MT`, `Vessel`. Identifiers (`registration`, `imo`) match under Rule 1.\n\n## Rule 6: nationality\n\nNationality is informational and does not confirm or rule out a match.\n\n## Output\n\n`/app/decisions.csv` with a header row `customer_id,decision,matched_uid`,\nexactly one row per customer in the batch, `decision` in `{MATCH, NO_MATCH}`,\nand `matched_uid` set to the entry `uid` for every `MATCH`. When more than one\nentry could match, choose the one supported by an identifier, then by a date\nof birth, then the first by `uid`.\n\n## Scoring\n\nThe batch is scored against hidden labels produced by the same process as\n`/app/dev/labels_dev.csv`. The task passes only if all of the following hold on\nthe batch: overall recall of true matches at least 0.97 and overall precision\nat least 0.97; recall at least 0.90 within every true-match variation class;\nfalse-positive rate at most 0.05 within every look-alike decoy class and at\nmost 0.01 among unrelated customers; and at least 0.97 of correct matches\ncarry the correct `matched_uid`. The development sample reports the same\nclasses so you can measure yourself before the batch is scored.\n  5828 customers.csv\n  2253 dev/customers_dev.csv\n  2253 dev/labels_dev.csv\n 10334 total\ncustomer_id,full_name,dob,nationality,id_type,id_number,type\r\nC004998,Johnny Schmitt,1968-05-17,FR,,,individual\r\nC005581,Tony O'Brien,1962-03-07,US,,,individual\r\nC004660,Bo Huang,1956-07-14,TW,,,individual\r\nC003390,Hsiao-Chun Hwang,1951-06-12,CN,,,individual\r\nC000737,Doctor,,SY,,,individual\r\nC004793,Yen Zhou,,SG,,,individual\r\nC002999,Bob Du Bois,1981-07-25,CA,,,individual\r\nC001615,M/T Silver Lining II,,LR,,,vessel\r\nC002837,Jamie Ferreyra,1975-01-22,BR,,,individual\r\nC004255,Hua Kwok,1981-03-26,CN,,,individual\r\nC000182,Victor Fedorov,1972-09-22,RU,,,individual\r\nC003161,Iryna Petrovna Kuznetsova,1974-08-21,BY,,,individual\r\nC005242,Yan Liu,1973-06-09,CN,,,individual\r\nC005785,Jen Pedersen,,CA,,,individual\r\nC002417,Pepe Lefevre,1997-01-02,BR,,,individual\r\ncustomer_id,full_name,dob,nationality,id_type,id_number,type\r\nD000484,Trish Kowalsky,,CA,,,individual\r\nD001992,Elisabeth Nguyễn,1952-11-03,CA,,,individual\r\nD001095,Onyx Minerals SA,,RU,,,entity\r\nD000024,Pepe Kowalsky,,MX,,,individual\r\nD000672,Abdul Rahman Shahin,,IQ,,,individual\r\nD000241,Hoseyn Ahmady,1999-04-02,AF,,,individual\r\nD000954,Big Mo,,IR,,,individual\r\nD001549,M/T Red Falcon One,,IR,,,vessel\r\nD000382,Abu Salem,1973-07-09,YE,,,individual\r\nD002081,Bob Petersen,1999-07-27,BR,,,individual\r\nD001905,Xiao Ming Liu,1996-03-02,CN,,,individual\r\nD001795,Jim Smithjones,1961-08-10,FR,,,individual\r\nD000911,Hussien Shahin,1986-12-26,YE,,,individual\r\nD001732,Fung Lam,1953-07-01,HK,,,individual\r\nD000629,Mehdy Tehrany,,IR,,,individual\r\nD000314,Zaitseva Tatiana,1960,IR,,,individual\r\nD001709,Xander García,1991-05-09,DE,,,individual\r\nD002192,Chun Lam,2000-08-28,SG,,,individual\r\nD000423,Ming Zhu,1959-09-14,SG,,,individual\r\ncustomer_id,expected_decision,expected_uid,class\r\nD000484,MATCH,SDN-10814,T1_translit\r\nD001992,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001095,NO_MATCH,,D4_entity_near_name\r\nD000024,MATCH,SDN-10030,T1_translit\r\nD000672,NO_MATCH,,D2_near_name\r\nD000241,MATCH,SDN-10394,T1_translit\r\nD000954,NO_MATCH,,D3_weak_alias_alone\r\nD001549,MATCH,SDN-11683,T8_vessel_prefix\r\nD000382,MATCH,SDN-10644,T5_alias_weak_corroborated\r\nD002081,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001905,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001795,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD000911,NO_MATCH,,D1_name_dob_conflict\r\nD001732,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD000629,MATCH,SDN-11077,T1_translit\r\nD000314,MATCH,SDN-10526,T3_structure\r\nD001709,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD002192,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD000423,MATCH,SDN-10720,T3_structure\r\nD000436,MATCH,SDN-10738,T3_structure\r\nD001678,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD000583,MATCH,SDN-11002,T6_id_exact\r\nD000347,MATCH,SDN-10589,T1_translit\r\nD001784,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001922,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001690,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD000028,MATCH,SDN-10035,T1_translit\r\nD001867,NO_MATCH,,R0_random\r\nD001130,NO_MATCH,,D4_entity_near_name\r\n<class 'list'> 1800\n{\n  \"uid\": \"SDN-10000\",\n  \"type\": \"individual\",\n  \"primary_name\": \"عبد الله الهاشمي\",\n  \"script_name\": \"عبد الله الهاشمي\",\n  \"aliases\": [],\n  \"dob\": \"1968-11-23\",\n  \"nationalities\": [\n    \"IQ\"\n  ],\n  \"ids\": [],\n  \"programs\": [\n    \"DPRK\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"uid\": \"SDN-10001\",\n  \"type\": \"individual\",\n  \"primary_name\": \"Muhammad al-Rashid\",\n  \"script_name\": \"محمد الرشيد\",\n  \"aliases\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mohamad Arrashid\",\n      \"strength\": \"strong\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Abu Omar\",\n      \"strength\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dob\": \"1973-09-08\",\n  \"nationalities\": [\n    \"AE\"\n  ],\n  \"ids\": [],\n  \"programs\": [\n    \"SYRIA\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"uid\": \"SDN-10002\",\n  \"type\": \"individual\",\n  \"primary_name\": \"Andrei Petrovich Yakovlev\",\n  \"script_name\": \"Андрей Петрович Яковлев\",\n  \"aliases\": [],\n  \"dob\": \"1958\",\n  \"nationalities\": [\n    \"RU\"\n  ],\n  \"ids\": [\